n or ahead.\n\nExpert raters mostly call the race Lean Republican, though a couple rate it Likely R and one calls it a tossup. Prediction markets remain skeptical of a Democratic upset, pricing Abbott near 80 percent. The forecast lands on a narrow Abbott lead of roughly three points, with meaningful uncertainty given the polling divergence and the state's low historical turnout volatility.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1819, "margin": -4.27}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2694, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2894, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2702, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2293, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2331, "margin": -3.3}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2978, "margin": -3.0}]}